rmulas here:\n\n1. Sum of products: (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) / 2.\n\n2. Arithmetic mean of products: [ (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) / 2 ] divided by C(n,2)=n(n-1)/2, so (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} over n(n-1).\n\nHence, the correct formula is:\n\n Arithmetic mean = [ (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ] / [n(n -1) ]\n\nTherefore, the formula should be [ (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ] / [n(n-1) ]\n\nWait, that\'s simpler. Let me verify with n=3:\n\n (6^2 -14)/ (3*2)=22/6=11/3≈3.666..., which matches the arithmetic mean. That is, the arithmetic mean is indeed [H_n^2 - H_n^{(2)} ] / [n(n-1) ]\n\nBut then why in the formula did we write:\n\n sum of products = (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) /2 and then arithmetic mean as sum of products / C(n,2). So,\n\n arithmetic mean = [ (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) /2 ] / [n(n-1)/2 ] = (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) / n(n-1)\n\nWhich is correct. So then why in the n=3 example, using this formula gives:\n\n (36 -14)/ (9)=22/9≈2.444..., but the actual arithmetic mean is 11/3≈3.666...\n\n Wait, there\'s a contradiction here. These two different results.\n\n Wait, unless I\'m misunderstanding, sum of products is (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} over 2, then arithmetic mean is that over C(n,2). So for sum of products: sp = (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) / 2.\n\n arithmetic mean = sp / C(n,2) = [ (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) /2 ] / [n(n-1)/2 ] = (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) /n(n-1)\n\nBut when we compute (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ), that equals to sum_{i<j}ij *2. Which was established earlier.\n\nWait, I must have messed up the definitions.\n\nLet me recap:\n\nLet S = sum_{1 ≤ i < j ≤n} ij.\n\nFrom the identity:\n\nsum_{k=1}^n k^2 = (sum_{k=1}^n k)^2 - 2S.\n\nTherefore, S = (sum k)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) / 2 = ( (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) / 2 = sum_{i<j} ij.\n\nSo sum of products (sum_{i<j} ij ) is equal to (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) /2.\n\nThus, arithmetic mean is sum_{i<j} ij / C(n,2 ) = [ (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) /2 ] / [n(n-1)/2 ] = (H_n)^2 - H_n^{(2)} ) /n(n-1)\n\nFor n=3:\n\n( (6)^2 -14 ) / 3(2) = (36-14)/6=22/6=11/3≈3.666..., which matches the arithmetic mean